From 8610d91835f1a096032f14f6c2d836d6cad562ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chenshuailin <chen.shuailin@intellif.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 09:26:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] port: allow LoRA + EAGLE/NEXTN/FROZEN_KV_MTP/DSPARK
 (generalize mtp_lora_phase1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

server_args.check_lora_server_args: relax the speculative-decoding LoRA gate
from ["NGRAM", None] to also allow EAGLE, NEXTN, FROZEN_KV_MTP and DSPARK.
Generalizes the fork's mtp_lora_phase1 allowlist (EAGLE/NEXTN/FROZEN_KV_MTP) by
adding DSPARK; DSPARK is a builtin SpeculativeAlgorithm (spec_info.py:36) that
otherwise hits the raise. EAGLE3 / DFLASH / STANDALONE stay blocked.

DSPARK+LoRA is target-verify-only (the adapter applies to the target/verify
forward; the DSPARK draft runs base weights, so accept-rate — not correctness —
degrades) and is PENDING FIRST GPU VALIDATION. This relaxation is inert unless a
DSPARK+LoRA launch is attempted; env-off byte-identical for every currently-used
config.

SCOPE / DEPENDENCY: only the allowlist is ported here (task d). The rest of
mtp_lora_phase1 — the per-runner `lora_enabled = enable_lora and not
is_draft_worker` gate + the fail-closed draft-runner LoRA audits — is NOT
ported. Without it, a DSPARK draft ModelRunner would init a LoRAManager under the
shared server_args.enable_lora (and the ported idle-LoRA suite gates on
server_args.enable_lora, not lora_enabled), so DSPARK+LoRA must not be run on GPU
until that gate lands. Flagged for the follow-up Phase-6 port.
---
 python/sglang/srt/server_args.py | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/server_args.py b/python/sglang/srt/server_args.py
index 2fd9010..81c4948 100644
--- a/python/sglang/srt/server_args.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/server_args.py
@@ -7069,10 +7069,35 @@ class ServerArgs:
                     f"so --max-loaded-loras must be less than or equal to double --max-loras-per-batch: {max_loaded_loras_limit}"
                 )
 
-            # Validate compatibility with speculative decoding
-            if self.speculative_algorithm not in ["NGRAM", None]:
+            # Validate compatibility with speculative decoding. Compared against
+            # the raw (post-CLI) algorithm name, consistent with the other
+            # `self.speculative_algorithm == "EAGLE"` checks in __post_init__.
+            # EAGLE/NEXTN, FROZEN_KV_MTP and DSPARK are allowed under the
+            # adapter-on-target-only design (vLLM PR #11966): the adapter applies
+            # to the target/verify forward only; the draft/MTP runner runs BASE
+            # weights, so correctness is owned by verify and only accept-rate (not
+            # correctness) degrades vs a LoRA-matched draft. EAGLE3 / DFLASH /
+            # STANDALONE remain blocked (unvalidated with LoRA).
+            #
+            # DSPARK+LoRA is TARGET-VERIFY-ONLY and PENDING FIRST GPU VALIDATION.
+            # It additionally REQUIRES the per-runner `lora_enabled` gate (the
+            # remainder of mtp_lora_phase1: lora_enabled = enable_lora and not
+            # is_draft_worker) so the DSPARK draft ModelRunner never inits a
+            # LoRAManager under the shared server_args. That gate is NOT in this
+            # commit, so this relaxation must stay unused on GPU until it lands.
+            if self.speculative_algorithm not in [
+                "NGRAM",
+                "EAGLE",
+                "NEXTN",
+                "FROZEN_KV_MTP",
+                "DSPARK",
+                None,
+            ]:
                 raise ValueError(
-                    "Currently LoRA is only compatible with NGRAM speculative decoding."
+                    "Currently LoRA is only compatible with NGRAM, EAGLE/NEXTN, "
+                    "FROZEN_KV_MTP, or DSPARK speculative decoding. Under neural-"
+                    "draft algorithms the LoRA adapter is applied to the target "
+                    "model only; draft models run base weights."
                 )
 
             # Parse lora_paths
